ggml-vulkan: the graph optimizer must not reorder a read past an in-place
write to the same tensor through a different view. Against llama.cpp 035e227;
apply from the source root with `patch -p1`.

ggml_vk_graph_optimize pulls later nodes ahead of earlier ones it judges
independent. Its dependency test saw a direct src edge, or two views of the
same tensor, but not a node that READS one view of a tensor while an earlier
node WRITES another view of it in place. In the hybrid recurrent cache that is
build_rs: an in-place SCALE by 0 zeroes a fresh state's row (a view of the
cache), and GET_ROWS then reads the states through another view. The
optimizer pulled GET_ROWS ahead of the zeroing, so a new sequence read the
previous request's state. The CPU backend runs nodes in insertion order and
never showed it.

Measured with `probes.py leak` (bench/lanes/engine-swap), Qwen3.5-4B MTP, -np 1:
  vanilla, Vulkan                         drift > 2 nats (':' -1.3108 on request 2)
  vanilla, CPU (-ngl 0)                   drift 0.0
  vanilla, GGML_VK_DISABLE_GRAPH_OPTIMIZE drift 0.0035
  this patch, optimizer on                drift 0.0035, the same five values
The 0.0035 left is separate (issue E2: stale attention-cache data, also
Vulkan-only, not flash attention); zeroing the attention data at slot start
takes it to 0.0.

--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp	2026-08-26 08:09:53.000000000 -0700
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp	2026-10-11 20:16:16.824193383 -0700
@@ -17550,6 +17550,22 @@
         if (dst2 == src2) {
             return true;
         }
+        // implicit dependency through an alias: dst reads memory that src
+        // writes (src is an in-place op on a view, dst reads another view of
+        // the same tensor), or dst writes memory that src reads. Without this
+        // the recurrent-state read (GET_ROWS on a view of the cache) could be
+        // pulled ahead of the in-place zeroing of a fresh state (SCALE on a
+        // row view of the same cache), and a new sequence read stale state.
+        for (uint32_t s = 0; s < GGML_MAX_SRC; ++s) {
+            const ggml_tensor *ds = dst->src[s];
+            if (ds && (ds->view_src ? ds->view_src : ds) == src2) {
+                return true;
+            }
+            const ggml_tensor *ss = src->src[s];
+            if (ss && (ss->view_src ? ss->view_src : ss) == dst2) {
+                return true;
+            }
+        }
         return false;
     };
 
